    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Celebrities with Degrees and Their Surprising Stories\ndate: 1995-01-01\n---\nCelebrities with Degrees and Their Surprising Stories\n\nHave you ever wondered what your favorite celebrities would be doing if they weren't in front of the camera, behind it, or constantly avoiding the paparazzi? It might surprise you to know that many of them are actually highly educated, and might even be considered geniuses. It might come as a shock to discover that numerous beloved celebrities pursued higher education thanks to the pythagorean theorem calculator assistance. The roster of celebrities possessing college diplomas is more extensive than anticipated. In this article, we will examine the academic institutions where a handful of notable individuals obtained their degrees and the subjects they specialized in.\n\nIndeed, this compilation demonstrates that not all individuals who enroll in college ultimately apply their degree directly to their occupation. Nevertheless, the valuable skills and knowledge acquired from attending college can still have a profound impact on one's life.\n\nHere is an overview of influential figures in the entertainment industry who initially pursued higher education, transitioning from television to film, singing to producing, and various other roles.\n\nMayim Bialik: Neuroscience\n\nIt has been discovered that Bialik possesses the same level of intelligence as the character she portrays on The Big Bang Theory. She successfully obtained a doctoral degree in neuroscience from the University of California, Los Angeles, where her research was centered around studying obsessive compulsive disorder in individuals with Prader-Willi syndrome, an uncommon condition caused by malfunctioning of the hypothalamus. This achievement not only highlights her acting talent but also underscores her significant academic contributions, making her a distinguished member among celebrities with degrees in science.\n\nNatalie Portman: Psychology\n\nNot widely acknowledged: Portman did not attend the debut of Star Wars: Phantom Menace as she was preparing for her high school exams. Despite being in high school, she managed to have two of her papers published in scientific journals. Eventually, she earned a Bachelor's degree in Psychology from Harvard University, , placing her among the esteemed list of celebrity Harvard graduates.\n\nPortman has stated that she is not concerned about the potential negative impact of college on her career, prioritizing intelligence over fame as her preference. However, it is evident that she has achieved success in both aspects, as demonstrated by her involvement in the renowned Star Wars movie franchise. Additionally, here is a comprehensive update on the latest information regarding Star Wars: Episode IX.\n\nEva Longoria: Kinesiology\n\nEva Longoria,"
